# Documentation and traceability

- **Source of truth for the spec:** `docs/requirements/items/` (one note per REQ / NFR / US / UAT / persona, with YAML frontmatter). Narrative files (`requirements.md`, `user-stories.md`, `uat-test-cases.md`) must be kept in sync.
- **IDs are never renumbered.** Deprecate with `spec_status: deprecated` and keep links bidirectional:
  - `REQ.stories` ↔ `US.requirements`;
  - `REQ.uat` ↔ `UAT.requirement`.
- **Tests:** name test suites and cases with the ids they verify, e.g. `describe('UAT-071 REQ-054 one invoice per pair', …)`.
- **UAT status:** when a UAT scenario passes in CI or on `dev`, set `status: Pass`, `last_run` and `tester` in `docs/requirements/items/uat/UAT-xxx.md` in the same PR.
- **Jira:**
  - every branch, commit and PR title starts with the Jira key `INT-xxx`;
  - do not copy requirement text into Jira; reference the ids.
  - Jira task codes such as `[REQ-0x]`, `[TD-0x]` are **project tasks**, not spec ids. Spec ids have three digits (`REQ-054`); technical decisions are `TD-1..TD-13`.
- **Mermaid:** flowchart, state, ER and class diagrams start with `%% elk %%`, one concern per diagram.
- Docs are in English. The deliverable is public (PU): no consortium-confidential content.
